      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To initiate the Drop-off tech process, the customer is first informed about canceling the order."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause initiates the process and describes the first two action steps."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Then, the question arises: has the order already been fulfilled?"
      ],
      "justification": "The question corresponds to the inquiry action and implicitly opens the XOR branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the answer is \"Yes,\""
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the positive branch condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "the bag is marked as returned in IS.",
        "If the bag is indeed returned, it is marked as such in IS."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps to the marking action; the second span redundantly restates the same step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "if the answer is \"No,\""
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the negative branch condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "the script(s) are marked as declined by the customer in IS.",
        "On the other hand, if the bag is not returned, the script(s) are marked as declined by the customer in IS."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps to the declining action; the second span redundantly restates the same step under a slightly different phrasing."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the bag is marked as returned in IS, the script bag is returned as well."
      ],
      "justification": "Describes the subsequent return step for the script bag."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Similarly, when the script(s) are marked as declined by the customer in IS, the script order is declined."
      ],
      "justification": "Describes the subsequent decline step for the script order."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "the customer notification is processed"
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the notification processing step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "the entire process comes to an end"
      ],
      "justification": "Signals the final step and the implicit termination of the workflow."
    }
  ],
